Summarise the conversation below so it can stand in for the original turns when
the conversation continues.

Keep what a later question might depend on:

- What the person is working on, and any constraint they stated
- Specific records already discussed, by name and reference
- Figures and dates already established, exactly as given
- Anything you were asked and could not answer, and why

Drop pleasantries, restatements, and your own explanations of how you found
things. Do not add anything that is not in the turns below, and do not resolve
anything that was left open.

Write it as notes, in the third person, under 200 words.

<atlas:context>
{% for turn in turns %}
Q: {{ turn.question }}
A: {{ turn.answer }}

{% endfor %}
</atlas:context>
